{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_468","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content harness/specs/rules/docs-sync.md -Raw | Select-Object -First 60; Write-Output \\\"=== referenced checks ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"docs-sync\\\" harness/specs scripts package.json --glob '\"'!*.json'\"' | Select-Object -First 20\"","aggregated_output":"---\nid: docs-sync\ntitle: Docs Sync\ntype: ai-coding-rule\nappliesTo:\n  - gateway-backend-communication\n---\n\nFunctional or architecture changes must explicitly declare whether README translation updates are required.\n\r\n=== referenced checks ===\r\nharness/specs\\scenarios\\gateway-backend-communication.md:37:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agency-role-memory-import.md:52:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agency-role-package-localization.md:54:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\scenarios\\sidebar-session-workgroup-drag-drop.md:8:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\scenarios\\gateway-startup-diagnostics.md:20:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agency-role-promotion-control-plane.md:59:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-avatar-orchestration-visuals.md:53:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\scenarios\\workspace-harness-bootstrap.md:18:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\scenarios\\windows-ui-v2.md:9:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-task-loop-mvp.md:35:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-dev-ecosystem-regularization.md:14:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-dev-ecosystem-regularization.md:50:- `harness/specs/rules/docs-sync.md`\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-dev-control-plane.md:34:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\browser-effect-provenance-boundary.md:25:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-reach-readers-integration.md:54:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\agent-dev-ecosystem-p0.md:33:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\boot-md-deprecation.md:23:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\browser-effect-session-type-provenance-boundary.md:23:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\capability-registry-v3-provider-native.md:63:  - docs-sync\r\nharness/specs\\tasks\\browser-effect-session-click-provenance-boundary.md:27:  - docs-sync\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_469","type":"reasoning","text":"The docs-sync rule only requires the change to *explicitly declare* whether README translation updates are required. My spec's frontmatter has `docs: required: true, files: [...]` — it declares docs requirements pointing to the closure doc. That satisfies the rule's spirit. There's no automated enforcement beyond the harness spec structure (which validates). Good — no README churn needed. I'll declare that in the final summary (no user-visible/README-level behavior change; the packet doc declares the docs requirement).\n\nHmm, to be explicit about docs-sync, maybe the spec should carry a note about README updates. The reference spec doesn't. It validated fine. Leave it.\n\nNow final verification pass. Let me run the complete battery once more cleanly and capture outputs for the summary:\n1. oracle-equivalent vitest (my test + guard) \n2. governance check\n3. scoped eslint\n4. typecheck web (already 0 after generating stubs)\n5. check-no-bom\n6. sums verify\n7. scratch: validate/dry-run/comms\n\nMost are already recorded. Let me do a final consolidated run of the workspace ones to have a clean final state confirmation, then finish.\n\nLet me also review my test file content once (print it) to ensure quality/format.\n\nThen compose the final answer as the RESULT_SCHEMA JSON.\n\nLet me print the test file and run the final battery."}}
